<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SActionScript version="1" name="plugin_native_editor_teardown_safe">

  <!-- fix/editor-ui-and-shortcuts, issue (a), second follow-up (2026-08-23):
       a SEPARATE, PRE-EXISTING crash found while investigating why a native
       editor "will not reopen". Unrelated to the FX-strip parenting bug in
       the same class: this one is reachable even from a single properly
       parented window, simply by never closing an open editor before the
       project (or the app) tears down — the ordinary shape of a real user
       just closing a project with a plugin window still up.

       ROOT CAUSE, found with gdb against this exact three-action script:
       SPluginNativeEditor connected its "close me when the slot dies"
       handler to the QObject BASE CLASS's own destroyed() signal. That
       signal fires from ~QObject(), which — being the base class — runs
       strictly AFTER ~SPluginSlot()'s own body and every MEMBER destructor,
       including proc_ (the std::shared_ptr holding the live plugin
       instance). So by the time destroyed() fired and the editor tried to
       close() -> closeEvent() -> twPluginEditor::detach(), the plugin was
       ALREADY DESTROYED — SIGSEGV inside twClapEditor::detach() touching a
       dangling CLAP GUI extension pointer.

       FIX PART 1: SPluginSlot gained a new signal, slotDestroying()
       (spluginslot.h), emitted as the FIRST statement of a (no longer
       =default) ~SPluginSlot() — while the slot, and the plugin behind it,
       are still fully alive. SPluginNativeEditor (and SPluginEffectStrip's
       generic editor, for consistency — see the note near the bottom) now
       connect to THIS instead of QObject::destroyed().

       FIX PART 2, found chasing a SECOND crash uncovered by fixing the
       first: closing an editor during project teardown correctly POSTS a
       deferred delete (QDialog::close() on a WA_DeleteOnClose widget), and
       a headless test-case run leaves through std::exit() with no event-loop pump in
       between — so that deferred ~QWidget()/~QWindow() ran from an atexit
       hook AFTER the platform integration had already torn down. Fixed by
       draining QEvent::DeferredDelete in smaragdOrderlyShutdown() (main.cpp),
       BEFORE std::exit(), while QApplication is still fully alive.

       THIS CASE DELIBERATELY VIOLATES plugin_native_editor.qxa's OWN STATED
       DISCIPLINE ("a case that opens one MUST close it") — that is the
       point: a forgetful caller, or a project simply being closed with an
       editor still open, must not crash the app. There is no explicit
       assertion for "the process did not segfault" — CTest catches that by
       EXIT CODE, the same mechanism that already catches
       qxa.split_plain_screenshot's teardown crash (see CLAUDE.md, "Two known
       crash flakes"). A PASS printed by the runner and then a non-zero exit
       is what a crash during teardown looks like from here.

       Watched failing (segfaulting), reliably and repeatedly, on the
       pre-fix binary — confirmed for BOTH fixes independently: reverting
       slotDestroying()'s connection alone crashes inside
       twClapEditor::detach() (proc_ already destroyed, exactly the trace
       above); restoring that fix but reverting the DeferredDelete drain
       crashes instead inside QWindow::~QWindow() at process exit, downstream
       of QOpenGLContext — the SAME symptom qxa.split_plain_screenshot
       already names as "a crash during teardown, after every action and
       assertion succeeded". A two-plugin variant of this repro (adding a
       SECOND track/slot for the generic editor) was tried first and did NOT
       reproduce reliably — a use-after-free's crash depends on allocator
       state, so it can silently read stale-but-harmless memory once the
       heap shape changes. This file is deliberately the SMALLEST script that
       reproduces every time.

       THE GENERIC EDITOR GOT THE SAME slotDestroying() SWITCH
       (splugineffectstrip.cpp) for CONSISTENCY, not because it independently
       crashes: SPluginParamEditor holds no ABI twPluginEditor to detach(),
       and a dedicated probe script (open the generic editor via
       plugin-generic-editor, never close it, let the project tear down)
       found NO repro under the old destroyed()-based connection either way.
       Not given its own crash gate here for exactly that reason — there is
       nothing observed to watch failing. -->

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gui"
                   name="Smaragd Test GUI" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <plugin-native-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="open" expectOpen="1"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
